      "text": "1. Given that the median of the set $\\{n, n + 5, n + 6, n + 9, n + 15\\}$ is 9, we can deduce the positions of the middle elements of the set.\n2. Since the median of a sorted set of 5 numbers is the 3rd number, we know that $n + 6 = 9$.\n3. Solving for $n$, we get $n = 3$.\n4. Substituting the value of $n$ into the set, we have $\\{3, 8, 9, 12, 18\\}$.\n5. To find the mean, we add up all the elements in the set and divide by $5$:\n   \\begin{align*}\n   \\text{Mean} &= \\frac{3 + 8 + 9 + 12 + 18}{5} \\\\\n   &= \\frac{50}{5} \\\\\n   &= \\boxed{10}.\n   \\end{align*}\nThe farthest point from the city is (90 miles) away in the northeast direction. Additionally, celestial observations reveal that the distance from the city is (2/3) of the distance from the farthest point. What is the approximate total distance from the city to the three locations mentioned?\n\nTo determine the distances from the city to each of the three locations, we start by calculating the distance from the city to the farthest point. According to the problem, this distance is 90 miles.\n\nNext, we are told that the distance from the city to the farthest point is \\(\\frac{2}{3}\\) of the distance from the city to a certain location. Let's denote the distance from the city to the certain location as \\(x\\). Therefore, we have:\n\\[\n\\frac{2}{3}x = 90\n\\]\nTo find \\(x\\), we solve the equation:\n\\[\nx = 90 \\times \\frac{3}{2} = 135\n\\]\nSo, the distance from the city to the certain location is 135 miles.\n\nNow, we need to find the distances to the other two locations. The set of locations mentioned are:\n1. The farthest point (90 miles).\n2. A location that is \\(\\frac{2}{5}\\) of the distance to the farthest point away in the northwest direction. Therefore, the distance to this location is:\n\\[\n\\frac{2}{5} \\times 90 = 36 \\text{ miles}\n\\]\n3. A location that is 15 miles due west of the city.\n\nThus, the distances from the city to the three locations are 90 miles, 36 miles, and 15 miles. The total distance from the city to these three locations is:\n\\[\n90 + 36 + 15 = 141 \\text{ miles}\n\\]\nTherefore, the approximate total distance from the city to the three locations is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{141}\n\\]",
