      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To find the mean of the set \\(\\{n, n + 5, n + 6, n + 9, n + 15\\}\\), we first need to determine the value of \\(n\\) using the information that the median is 9.\n\nThe median of a set of five numbers is the third number when the numbers are arranged in ascending order. The set \\(\\{n, n + 5, n + 6, n + 9, n + 15\\}\\) is already in ascending order. Therefore, the median is the third number, which is \\(n + 6\\).\n\nGiven that the median is 9, we can set up the equation:\n\\[\nn + 6 = 9\n\\]\nSolving for \\(n\\), we get:\n\\[\nn = 9 - 6 = 3\n\\]\n\nNow that we have the value of \\(n\\), we can find the elements of the set:\n\\[\n\\{n, n + 5, n + 6, n + 9, n + 15\\} = \\{3, 8, 9, 12, 18\\}\n\\]\n\nNext, we calculate the mean of this set. The mean is the sum of the elements divided by the number of elements. The sum of the elements is:\n\\[\n3 + 8 + 9 + 12 + 18 = 50\n\\]\nSince there are 5 elements in the set, the mean is:\n\\[\n\\text{Mean} = \\frac{50}{5} = 10\n\\]\n\nThus, the mean of the set is \\(\\boxed{10}\\).",
